   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Monte Carlo Simulation Basics\n",
    "\n",
    "**Runtime:** ~8 minutes  \n",
    "**Level:** Beginner\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook introduces Monte Carlo simulation for strategy robustness testing.\n",
    "\n",
    "## What is Monte Carlo Simulation?\n",
    "\n",
    "Monte Carlo simulation tests strategy robustness by:\n",
    "- **Data Permutation**: Randomly shuffling historical data sequences\n",
    "- **Noise Infusion**: Adding realistic market noise to test parameters\n",
    "- **Distribution Analysis**: Understanding the range of possible outcomes\n",
    "\n",
    "## Why Use Monte Carlo?\n",
    "\n",
    "- ✅ **Stress Testing**: See how strategies perform under different scenarios\n",
    "- ✅ **Confidence Intervals**: Understand the range of expected returns\n",
    "- ✅ **Overfitting Detection**: Strategies that break down with noise are likely overfit\n",
    "- ✅ **Risk Assessment**: Understand worst-case and best-case scenarios"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "**📋 Notebook Information**\n",
    "\n",
    "- **RustyBT Version:** 0.1.2+\n",
    "- **Last Validated:** 2025-11-07\n",
    "- **API Compatibility:** Verified ✅\n",
    "- **Documentation:** [Monte Carlo API Reference](https://rustybt.readthedocs.io/en/latest/api/)\n",
    "\n",
    "---"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Setup\n",
    "from rustybt.analytics import setup_notebook\n",
    "setup_notebook()\n",
    "\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import plotly.graph_objects as go\n",
    "from plotly.subplots import make_subplots\n",
    "from datetime import datetime\n",
    "\n",
    "from rustybt import TradingAlgorithm\n",
    "from rustybt.optimization.monte_carlo import (\n",
    "    MonteCarloSimulator,\n",
    "    DataPermutationSimulator,\n",
    "    PermutationMethod,\n",
    ")\n",
    "from rustybt.optimization.noise_infusion import (\n",
    "    NoiseInfusionSimulator,\n",
    "    NoiseConfig,\n",
    "    NoiseType,\n",
    ")\n",
    "from rustybt.analytics import plot_equity_curve\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"✓ Imports successful\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Define a Simple Strategy\n",
    "\n",
    "Let's start with a basic moving average crossover strategy."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "class MovingAverageCrossover(TradingAlgorithm):\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Simple moving average crossover strategy.\n",
    "    \n",
    "    Buy when fast MA crosses above slow MA.\n",
    "    Sell when fast MA crosses below slow MA.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    \n",
    "    params = {\n",
    "        'fast_window': 20,\n",
    "        'slow_window': 50,\n",
    "    }\n",
    "    \n",
    "    def initialize(self, context):\n",
    "        context.asset = self.symbol('SPY')\n",
    "        context.fast_window = self.params['fast_window']\n",
    "        context.slow_window = self.params['slow_window']\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # Schedule daily rebalance\n",
    "        self.schedule_function(\n",
    "            self.check_signal,\n",
    "            date_rules=self.date_rules.every_day(),\n",
    "            time_rules=self.time_rules.market_open()\n",
    "        )\n",
    "    \n",
    "    def check_signal(self, context, data):\n",
    "        if not data.can_trade(context.asset):\n",
    "            return\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # Get price history\n",
    "        prices = data.history(\n",
    "            context.asset,\n",
    "            'close',\n",
    "            context.slow_window + 1,\n",
    "            '1d'\n",
    "        )\n",
    "        \n",
    "        if len(prices) < context.slow_window + 1:\n",
    "            return\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # Calculate moving averages\n",
    "        fast_ma = prices[-context.fast_window:].mean()\n",
    "        slow_ma = prices[-context.slow_window:].mean()\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # Previous values for crossover detection\n",
    "        fast_ma_prev = prices[-(context.fast_window+1):-1].mean()\n",
    "        slow_ma_prev = prices[-(context.slow_window+1):-1].mean()\n",
    "        \n",
    "        current_position = context.portfolio.positions[context.asset].amount\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # Golden cross: fast crosses above slow (buy signal)\n",
    "        if fast_ma > slow_ma and fast_ma_prev <= slow_ma_prev:\n",
    "            if current_position <= 0:\n",
    "                self.order_target_percent(context.asset, 1.0)\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # Death cross: fast crosses below slow (sell signal)\n",
    "        elif fast_ma < slow_ma and fast_ma_prev >= slow_ma_prev:\n",
    "            if current_position > 0:\n",
    "                self.order_target_percent(context.asset, 0.0)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"✓ Strategy defined\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Run Baseline Backtest\n",
    "\n",
    "First, run the strategy on historical data to get a baseline."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Note: Requires data bundle setup (see 02_data_ingestion.ipynb)\n",
    "#\n",
    "# from rustybt.utils.run_algo import run_algorithm\n",
    "#\n",
    "# baseline_results = run_algorithm(\n",
    "#     start=pd.Timestamp('2020-01-01', tz='utc'),\n",
    "#     end=pd.Timestamp('2023-12-31', tz='utc'),\n",
    "#     initialize=MovingAverageCrossover().initialize,\n",
    "#     handle_data=MovingAverageCrossover().handle_data,\n",
    "#     capital_base=100000.0,\n",
    "#     bundle='yfinance',\n",
    "#     data_frequency='daily',\n",
    "# )\n",
    "#\n",
    "# print(f\"Baseline Sharpe Ratio: {baseline_results['sharpe_ratio'].iloc[-1]:.3f}\")\n",
    "# print(f\"Baseline Total Return: {baseline_results['total_return'].iloc[-1]:.2%}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Monte Carlo Data Permutation\n",
    "\n",
    "Test strategy robustness by randomly shuffling historical data sequences."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Create Monte Carlo simulator with data permutation\n",
    "mc_simulator = DataPermutationSimulator(\n",
    "    n_simulations=100,  # Run 100 Monte Carlo simulations\n",
    "    method=PermutationMethod.BLOCK_BOOTSTRAP,  # Preserve temporal structure\n",
    "    block_size=20,  # 20-day blocks\n",
    "    seed=42,  # Reproducible results\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Run Monte Carlo simulation\n",
    "# mc_results = mc_simulator.run(\n",
    "#     strategy_class=MovingAverageCrossover,\n",
    "#     params={'fast_window': 20, 'slow_window': 50},\n",
    "#     bundle='yfinance',\n",
    "#     start_date=datetime(2020, 1, 1),\n",
    "#     end_date=datetime(2023, 12, 31),\n",
    "# )\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"✓ Monte Carlo simulator configured\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Analyze Monte Carlo Results\n",
    "\n",
    "Visualize the distribution of outcomes from Monte Carlo simulations."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def analyze_monte_carlo_results(mc_results, baseline_sharpe):\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Analyze and visualize Monte Carlo simulation results.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    # Extract Sharpe ratios from all simulations\n",
    "    sharpe_ratios = [sim.metrics['sharpe_ratio'] for sim in mc_results.simulations]\n",
    "    total_returns = [sim.metrics['total_return'] for sim in mc_results.simulations]\n",
    "    max_drawdowns = [sim.metrics['max_drawdown'] for sim in mc_results.simulations]\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Calculate statistics\n",
    "    sharpe_mean = np.mean(sharpe_ratios)\n",
    "    sharpe_std = np.std(sharpe_ratios)\n",
    "    sharpe_median = np.median(sharpe_ratios)\n",
    "    sharpe_5th = np.percentile(sharpe_ratios, 5)\n",
    "    sharpe_95th = np.percentile(sharpe_ratios, 95)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Print summary\n",
    "    print(\"\\n=== Monte Carlo Results Summary ===\")\n",
    "    print(f\"Number of simulations: {len(sharpe_ratios)}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"\\nSharpe Ratio:\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  Baseline:       {baseline_sharpe:.3f}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  Mean:           {sharpe_mean:.3f}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  Median:         {sharpe_median:.3f}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  Std Dev:        {sharpe_std:.3f}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  5th percentile: {sharpe_5th:.3f}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  95th percentile: {sharpe_95th:.3f}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"\\n% of simulations with Sharpe > 0: {sum(s > 0 for s in sharpe_ratios) / len(sharpe_ratios):.1%}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"% of simulations exceeding baseline: {sum(s > baseline_sharpe for s in sharpe_ratios) / len(sharpe_ratios):.1%}\")\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Create visualizations\n",
    "    fig = make_subplots(\n",
    "        rows=2, cols=2,\n",
    "        subplot_titles=(\n",
    "            'Sharpe Ratio Distribution',\n",
    "            'Total Return Distribution',\n",
    "            'Max Drawdown Distribution',\n",
    "            'Sharpe vs Return Scatter'\n",
    "        ),\n",
    "        specs=[\n",
    "            [{'type': 'histogram'}, {'type': 'histogram'}],\n",
    "            [{'type': 'histogram'}, {'type': 'scatter'}]\n",
    "        ]\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Sharpe ratio histogram\n",
    "    fig.add_trace(\n",
    "        go.Histogram(\n",
    "            x=sharpe_ratios,\n",
    "            nbinsx=30,\n",
    "            name='Sharpe Ratio',\n",
    "            marker_color='blue',\n",
    "            opacity=0.7\n",
    "        ),\n",
    "        row=1, col=1\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Add baseline line\n",
    "    fig.add_vline(\n",
    "        x=baseline_sharpe,\n",
    "        line_dash=\"dash\",\n",
    "        line_color=\"red\",\n",
    "        annotation_text=\"Baseline\",\n",
    "        row=1, col=1\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Total return histogram\n",
    "    fig.add_trace(\n",
    "        go.Histogram(\n",
    "            x=total_returns,\n",
    "            nbinsx=30,\n",
    "            name='Total Return',\n",
    "            marker_color='green',\n",
    "            opacity=0.7\n",
    "        ),\n",
    "        row=1, col=2\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Max drawdown histogram\n",
    "    fig.add_trace(\n",
    "        go.Histogram(\n",
    "            x=max_drawdowns,\n",
    "            nbinsx=30,\n",
    "            name='Max Drawdown',\n",
    "            marker_color='red',\n",
    "            opacity=0.7\n",
    "        ),\n",
    "        row=2, col=1\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Sharpe vs Return scatter\n",
    "    fig.add_trace(\n",
    "        go.Scatter(\n",
    "            x=sharpe_ratios,\n",
    "            y=total_returns,\n",
    "            mode='markers',\n",
    "            name='Simulations',\n",
    "            marker=dict(color='blue', size=5, opacity=0.5)\n",
    "        ),\n",
    "        row=2, col=2\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    \n",
    "    fig.update_xaxes(title_text=\"Sharpe Ratio\", row=1, col=1)\n",
    "    fig.update_xaxes(title_text=\"Total Return\", row=1, col=2)\n",
    "    fig.update_xaxes(title_text=\"Max Drawdown\", row=2, col=1)\n",
    "    fig.update_xaxes(title_text=\"Sharpe Ratio\", row=2, col=2)\n",
    "    fig.update_yaxes(title_text=\"Count\", row=1, col=1)\n",
    "    fig.update_yaxes(title_text=\"Count\", row=1, col=2)\n",
    "    fig.update_yaxes(title_text=\"Count\", row=2, col=1)\n",
    "    fig.update_yaxes(title_text=\"Total Return\", row=2, col=2)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    fig.update_layout(\n",
    "        height=800,\n",
    "        title_text=\"Monte Carlo Simulation Analysis\",\n",
    "        showlegend=False\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    \n",
    "    return fig\n",
    "\n",
    "# Example usage:\n",
    "# fig = analyze_monte_carlo_results(mc_results, baseline_sharpe=1.2)\n",
    "# fig.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"✓ Analysis function defined\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Noise Infusion Testing\n",
    "\n",
    "Add realistic market noise to test parameter stability."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Configure noise infusion\n",
    "noise_config = NoiseConfig(\n",
    "    noise_type=NoiseType.MULTIPLICATIVE,  # Percentage-based noise\n",
    "    noise_level=0.02,  # 2% noise\n",
    "    seed=42,\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create noise infusion simulator\n",
    "noise_simulator = NoiseInfusionSimulator(\n",
    "    n_simulations=100,\n",
    "    noise_config=noise_config,\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Run noise infusion tests\n",
    "# noise_results = noise_simulator.run(\n",
    "#     strategy_class=MovingAverageCrossover,\n",
    "#     params={'fast_window': 20, 'slow_window': 50},\n",
    "#     bundle='yfinance',\n",
    "#     start_date=datetime(2020, 1, 1),\n",
    "#     end_date=datetime(2023, 12, 31),\n",
    "# )\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"✓ Noise infusion simulator configured\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Noise type: {noise_config.noise_type.value}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Noise level: {noise_config.noise_level:.1%}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Noise Infusion Interpretation\n",
    "\n",
    "**What to look for:**\n",
    "- **Tight distribution**: Strategy is robust to parameter variations\n",
    "- **Wide distribution**: Strategy is sensitive to small changes\n",
    "- **Mean << Baseline**: Strategy is likely overfit to specific parameters"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def compare_robustness(mc_results, noise_results, baseline_metrics):\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Compare robustness between data permutation and noise infusion.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    # Extract Sharpe ratios\n",
    "    mc_sharpes = [s.metrics['sharpe_ratio'] for s in mc_results.simulations]\n",
    "    noise_sharpes = [s.metrics['sharpe_ratio'] for s in noise_results.simulations]\n",
    "    baseline_sharpe = baseline_metrics['sharpe_ratio']\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Create comparison plot\n",
    "    fig = go.Figure()\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Monte Carlo distribution\n",
    "    fig.add_trace(go.Histogram(\n",
    "        x=mc_sharpes,\n",
    "        name='Data Permutation',\n",
    "        opacity=0.6,\n",
    "        marker_color='blue',\n",
    "        nbinsx=30\n",
    "    ))\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Noise infusion distribution\n",
    "    fig.add_trace(go.Histogram(\n",
    "        x=noise_sharpes,\n",
    "        name='Noise Infusion',\n",
    "        opacity=0.6,\n",
    "        marker_color='green',\n",
    "        nbinsx=30\n",
    "    ))\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Baseline line\n",
    "    fig.add_vline(\n",
    "        x=baseline_sharpe,\n",
    "        line_dash=\"dash\",\n",
    "        line_color=\"red\",\n",
    "        annotation_text=\"Baseline\"\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    \n",
    "    fig.update_layout(\n",
    "        title=\"Robustness Comparison: Data Permutation vs Noise Infusion\",\n",
    "        xaxis_title=\"Sharpe Ratio\",\n",
    "        yaxis_title=\"Count\",\n",
    "        barmode='overlay',\n",
    "        height=500\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Print statistics\n",
    "    print(\"\\n=== Robustness Comparison ===\")\n",
    "    print(f\"Baseline Sharpe: {baseline_sharpe:.3f}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"\\nData Permutation:\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  Mean:   {np.mean(mc_sharpes):.3f}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  Std:    {np.std(mc_sharpes):.3f}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  CV:     {np.std(mc_sharpes) / abs(np.mean(mc_sharpes)):.3f}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"\\nNoise Infusion:\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  Mean:   {np.mean(noise_sharpes):.3f}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  Std:    {np.std(noise_sharpes):.3f}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  CV:     {np.std(noise_sharpes) / abs(np.mean(noise_sharpes)):.3f}\")\n",
    "    \n",
    "    return fig\n",
    "\n",
    "# Example usage:\n",
    "# fig = compare_robustness(mc_results, noise_results, baseline_results)\n",
    "# fig.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"✓ Comparison function defined\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Confidence Intervals\n",
    "\n",
    "Calculate confidence intervals for strategy metrics."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def calculate_confidence_intervals(mc_results, confidence_level=0.95):\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Calculate confidence intervals from Monte Carlo results.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    alpha = 1 - confidence_level\n",
    "    lower_percentile = (alpha / 2) * 100\n",
    "    upper_percentile = (1 - alpha / 2) * 100\n",
    "    \n",
    "    metrics = {\n",
    "        'sharpe_ratio': [s.metrics['sharpe_ratio'] for s in mc_results.simulations],\n",
    "        'total_return': [s.metrics['total_return'] for s in mc_results.simulations],\n",
    "        'max_drawdown': [s.metrics['max_drawdown'] for s in mc_results.simulations],\n",
    "        'volatility': [s.metrics['volatility'] for s in mc_results.simulations],\n",
    "    }\n",
    "    \n",
    "    intervals = {}\n",
    "    \n",
    "    print(f\"\\n=== {confidence_level:.0%} Confidence Intervals ===\")\n",
    "    \n",
    "    for metric_name, values in metrics.items():\n",
    "        mean = np.mean(values)\n",
    "        lower = np.percentile(values, lower_percentile)\n",
    "        upper = np.percentile(values, upper_percentile)\n",
    "        \n",
    "        intervals[metric_name] = {\n",
    "            'mean': mean,\n",
    "            'lower': lower,\n",
    "            'upper': upper,\n",
    "        }\n",
    "        \n",
    "        print(f\"\\n{metric_name}:\")\n",
    "        print(f\"  Mean:  {mean:.3f}\")\n",
    "        print(f\"  Range: [{lower:.3f}, {upper:.3f}]\")\n",
    "    \n",
    "    return intervals\n",
    "\n",
    "# Example usage:\n",
    "# intervals = calculate_confidence_intervals(mc_results, confidence_level=0.95)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"✓ Confidence interval function defined\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Summary\n",
    "\n",
    "### Key Takeaways\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Monte Carlo simulation** provides confidence intervals for strategy performance\n",
    "2. **Data permutation** tests robustness to different market sequences\n",
    "3. **Noise infusion** tests sensitivity to parameter variations\n",
    "4. **Tight distributions** indicate robust strategies\n",
    "5. **Wide distributions** or **mean << baseline** suggest overfitting\n",
    "\n",
    "### Interpretation Guide\n",
    "\n",
    "**Robust Strategy:**\n",
    "- ✅ 90%+ simulations profitable\n",
    "- ✅ Mean close to baseline (within 20%)\n",
    "- ✅ Narrow confidence intervals\n",
    "- ✅ Similar results across permutation and noise tests\n",
    "\n",
    "**Overfit Strategy:**\n",
    "- ❌ <50% simulations profitable\n",
    "- ❌ Mean significantly below baseline\n",
    "- ❌ Wide confidence intervals\n",
    "- ❌ High sensitivity to noise\n",
    "\n",
    "### Best Practices\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Run sufficient simulations**: Use at least 100 simulations\n",
    "2. **Test multiple noise levels**: Try 1%, 2%, 5% noise\n",
    "3. **Compare methods**: Use both data permutation and noise infusion\n",
    "4. **Set thresholds**: Require mean > 80% of baseline\n",
    "5. **Document results**: Save confidence intervals for reporting\n",
    "\n",
    "### Next Steps\n",
    "\n",
    "- Notebook 16: Sensitivity Analysis Basics\n",
    "- Notebook 17: Genetic Algorithm Basics\n",
    "- Notebook 24: Monte Carlo + Portfolio Optimization\n",
    "\n",
    "### Resources\n",
    "\n",
    "- [Monte Carlo Documentation](https://rustybt.readthedocs.io/en/latest/optimization/monte-carlo/)\n",
    "- [Noise Infusion Guide](https://rustybt.readthedocs.io/en/latest/optimization/noise-infusion/)\n",
    "- [Robustness Testing Best Practices](https://rustybt.readthedocs.io/en/latest/guides/robustness/)"
   ]
  }
 ],
